      "analysis_source": "llm-per-reviewer",
      "patch_summary": "This patch series makes the queue depths in the ARM SMMUv3 IOMMU tunable, allowing them to be adjusted based on system requirements. The queues are currently sized from the IDR1 maximum and allocated at probe, which can consume megabytes of memory per queue per SMMU instance. In a kdump kernel, this can lead to out-of-memory errors due to limited crashkernel reservations. The patch series introduces a module parameter cmdq_max_n_shift that allows the command queue depth to be adjusted, and applies it in non-kdump kernels. This reduces the memory consumption of the queues from megabytes to kilobytes, allowing kdump kernels to save vmcores successfully."
